[49m[39m  106, 106[0m:[39m[49m ## Feature combinations
[0m[49m[39m  107, 107[0m:[39m[49m 
[0m[49m[39m  108, 108[0m:[39m[49m `translation/Cargo.toml` has no `[features]` table, therefore the only
[0m[49m[39m  109, 109[0m:[39m[49m combination is the default one:
[0m[49m[39m  110, 110[0m:[39m[49m 
[0m[49m[39m  111, 111[0m:[39m[49m ```
[0m[49m[39m  112, 112[0m:[39m[49m default (no features)
[0m[49m[39m  113, 113[0m:[39m[49m ```
[0m[49m[39m  114, 114[0m:[39m[49m 
[0m[49m[39m  115, 115[0m:[39m[49m `tests/feature_matrix.sh` enumerates the feature list from `Cargo.toml` and runs
[0m[49m[38;5;9m- 116     [0m:[38;5;9m[49m `cargo test` for every combination; with zero declared features it runs the
[0m[49m[38;5;9m- 117     [0m:[38;5;9m[49m single default configuration plus `--no-default-features`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      116[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `cargo check` / `cargo build --release` / `cargo test --release` plus an `nm -D`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      117[0m:[38;5;10m[49m symbol diff for every combination; with zero declared features it verifies the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      118[0m:[38;5;10m[49m default configuration and `--no-default-features`.  Both pass with an empty
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      119[0m:[38;5;10m[49m symbol diff.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      120[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      121[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## What the differential comparison actually compares
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      122[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      123[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Pointers differ between the two libraries by construction, so every row is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      124[0m:[38;5;10m[49m compared through a canonical structural dump (`tests/common/mod.rs`):
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      125[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      126[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `stbds_array_header`: `length`, `capacity`, `temp`, and whether `hash_table`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      127[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   is set;
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      128[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * every live element, byte for byte — with a `char *` key rendered as the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      129[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   *pointed-to string* so that `STRDUP`/`ARENA` copies compare by content;
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      130[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `stbds_hash_index`: `slot_count`, `used_count`, both thresholds,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      131[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `tombstone_count`, `tombstone_count_threshold`, `seed`, `slot_count_log2`, and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      132[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   the embedded `stbds_string_arena`'s `remaining` / `block` / `mode`;
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      133[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * the `STBDS_ALIGN_FWD` result for `storage` as three address-independent
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      134[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   predicates (64-byte aligned, inside the over-allocated padding);
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      135[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * every bucket's full `hash[8]` and `index[8]` array;
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      136[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * for `str_put`, the bytes written to fd 1, captured in a forked child.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      137[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      138[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Two fields are deliberately excluded because the C leaves them
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      139[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **uninitialised**, so they hold different heap garbage in the two processes:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      140[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      141[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `stbds_hash_index::temp_key` after a rehash — `stbds_make_hash_index` never
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      142[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   writes it and only copies `string` and `seed` from the old table.  Tests prime
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      143[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   it to `0` before a `hmput_key` call and compare it only when that call did not
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      144[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   rehash, which turns "did the library write `temp_key`?" into an observable
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      145[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   fact (this is what makes rows 21/22 of `ERRORS.md` testable).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      146[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * element bytes outside the key region — `hmput_key` only writes the key, the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      147[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `stbds_hmput` macro writes the value.  The tests perform that value store
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      148[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   themselves (`fill_value`) so the whole element becomes defined.
